# This is a monorepo — there is no root .env.
#
# Each app reads its own file, from its own working directory:
#
#   apps/api/.env          NestJS API.  See apps/api/.env.example
#                          (PM2 starts it with cwd ./apps/api, so a root .env
#                          would simply not be read.)
#
#   apps/web/.env.local    Next.js site (development).
#   apps/web/.env.production   Next.js site (live values, committed).
#                          See apps/web/.env.example
#
# This file used to hold a half-copy of the API variables, including AWS_*
# storage names the code never reads and a stale NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL port. It is
# kept only as a signpost so nobody copies those again.
#
# Quick start:
#   cp apps/api/.env.example apps/api/.env
#   cp apps/web/.env.example apps/web/.env.local
#   npm install && npm run build        # always from this folder (turborepo)
